Interview Experience – Societe Generale  | Role: DevOps Engineer

Below are the questions discussed 👇

• Can you introduce yourself and explain your current DevOps responsibilities?
• What does a normal production day look like for you as a DevOps engineer?
• How do you collaborate with developers to release changes safely?

CI/CD & Automation
• How do you design a CI/CD pipeline that supports frequent releases without breaking production?
• What checks do you include before allowing a deployment to production?
• How do you handle failed deployments in a live environment?
• What is your rollback strategy if a release causes issues?

Kubernetes & Containers
• How do you troubleshoot a pod that is stuck in Pending state?
• What causes frequent pod restarts, and how do you debug them?
• How do you manage application configuration in Kubernetes?
• How do you expose applications securely from a Kubernetes cluster?

Linux & System Operations
• A server suddenly becomes slow — how do you identify the root cause?
• How do you check disk space issues and prevent outages caused by it?
• What steps do you follow when a service fails after a reboot?

Cloud & Security
• How do you restrict access to cloud resources in a shared environment?
• How do you secure secrets used by applications and pipelines?
• What practices do you follow to keep cloud environments compliant?

Monitoring & Reliability
• What metrics and alerts do you consider critical for production systems?
• How do you differentiate between noise and actionable alerts?

Version Control
• How do you manage Git branching in a team environment?
• How do you handle hotfixes directly in production?

📌 The focus was more on practical experience and decision-making rather than theoretical definitions.
